 17592186045417] [17592186491067 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491067 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186490928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491067 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a38d7fe4-d3d9-5f07-8a46-a68180a20afb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491068 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186490564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491068 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186490584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491068 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186490736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491068 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186490783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491068 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186490903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491068 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491068 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491068 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186490736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491068 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a928408c-e2bb-5ac3-8926-8be8d60e417f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491081 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186490512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491081 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186490643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491081 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186490770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491081 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186490897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491081 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186490936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491081 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491081 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491081 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186490897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491081 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c686f557-e13f-5945-8efd-5e2a53507af7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491183 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491183 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143489" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491183 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491183 #edb/ref 1071 "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ of $n$ coins is drawn from a population. The population has coins of two different denominations, $$1$ and $$0.50,$ distributed in the ratio $1:4.$ Determine the smallest sample size required so that the standard error of the mean is less than $$0.02.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491183 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9f4e58b8-0514-5aa4-9211-b553375a01af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491183 #edb/ref 1074 "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the coins in the population have denominations $$1$ and $$0.50,$ and these are distributed in the ratio $1:4.$ Therefore, to compute the population's mean and variance, we can consider a population consisting of $1+4=5$ coins only with the following denominations:\n\n$$\n$1,\\,$0.5,\\,$0.5,\\,$0.5,\\,$0.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(1+4\\cdot 0.5) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(1+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =$0.6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}^{2}-{\\mu }^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({1}^{2}+4\\cdot {0.5}^{2})-{0.6}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2)-0.36 \\\\  & =0.4-0.36 \\\\  & =0.04.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the population standard deviation is $\\sigma =\\sqrt{0.04}=0.2,$ and we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{0.2}{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe require that the standard error is less than $$0.02.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{0.2}{\\sqrt{n}} & <0.02 \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\frac{0.2}{0.02} \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >10 \\\\ n & >{10}^{2} \\\\ n & >100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest sample size is $n=101.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491224 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186491278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491224 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "145bbf22-1749-5090-aadc-e3554ab59101" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491224 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186491194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491233 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186491274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491233 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "46254631-f53c-514a-8d4a-8cae395482d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491233 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186491183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491271 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186491224 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491271 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e09f4a70-dbb4-5510-9c9f-f62ce6e6b9da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491271 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491274 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f623e816-8a9f-53dc-ac9b-5d259ddbb546" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491274 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186491123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491278 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186491233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491278 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "faa8d334-a6c2-5d81-9e07-13cab6f2da50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491278 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186491203 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
